.TH SCROLLWM 1 "March 2026" "scrollwm 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scrollwm \- experimental scrollable tiling window manager for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scrollwm
.RI [ --verbose ]
.RI [ --log-file " PATH" ]
.RI [ --sync ]
.RI [ --check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scrollwm
is an experimental, keyboard-first tiling window manager for X11/XLibre.
It arranges windows in a scrollable linear layout and supports multiple workspaces,
runtime layout direction toggling, fullscreen restore semantics, and configurable keybindings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check
Validate X11 connectivity and exit (does not attempt to become WM).
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BI --log-file " PATH"
Append logs to PATH while continuing to log to standard error.
.TP
.B --sync
Enable synchronous X11 request behavior using
.B LIBXCB_SYNCHRONIZE=1
for diagnostics.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is loaded from:
.PP
.I ~/.config/scrollwm/config.toml
.PP
If the file is missing, built-in defaults are used.
.SH DEFAULT KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Mod+Enter
Launch terminal
.TP
.B Mod+j / Mod+k
Focus next / previous window
.TP
.B Mod+1..4
Switch workspace
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+1..4
Move focused window to workspace
.TP
.B Mod+Space
Toggle layout direction (horizontal/vertical)
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+j / Mod+Shift+k
Reorder focused window in scroll order
.TP
.B Mod+f
Toggle fullscreen on focused tiled window
.TP
.B Mod+q
Close focused window via WM_DELETE_WINDOW
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+e
Exit ScrollWM
.SH SESSION INTEGRATION
For display manager sessions, use:
.PP
.B scrollwm-session
.PP
which optionally starts picom according to config and then execs
.BR scrollwm .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/xsessions/scrollwm.desktop
Display manager desktop entry.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/scrollwm/config.toml.example
Example configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B scrollwm
returns 0 on normal exit and non-zero on startup/runtime failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scrollwm-session (1)
.SH AUTHORS
ScrollWM contributors.
